From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: msdelta: the delta API refuses with an error instead of killing the caller

Every msdelta export was a bare stub. Microsoft 365's Click-to-Run service
updates its own files from deltas: it called ApplyDeltaB and was killed
mid-install. Applying a delta is still not implemented; ApplyDelta{A,W,B},
ApplyDeltaProvidedB and GetDeltaInfo{A,W,B} return FALSE with
ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, so a caller falls back to the whole file, and
DeltaFree succeeds. The 32-bit spec pops the by-value DELTA_INPUTs.

--- a/dlls/msdelta/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/msdelta/Makefile.in
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
 MODULE    = msdelta.dll
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
+
+SOURCES = \
+	msdelta.c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/msdelta/msdelta.c
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+/*
+ * msdelta: Stained Glass OS -- the delta (PA30) API refuses cleanly
+ *
+ * Every export was a bare stub, and a program that called one was killed
+ * ("unimplemented function msdelta.dll.ApplyDeltaB, aborting"): Microsoft
+ * 365's Click-to-Run service updates its own files from deltas and died
+ * mid-install. Applying a delta is not implemented yet; these report that
+ * as an error, so a caller can fall back to the whole file, as it must when
+ * a delta does not apply.
+ *
+ * Copyright (C) 2026 Stained Glass OS contributors
+ *
